#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:179
msgid "Useful transform flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:181
msgid ""
"The ``mmetl transform slack`` command supports several optional flags "
"that can help with common migration scenarios:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:183
msgid ""
"``--skip-attachments`` / ``-a``: Skip copying attachments from the import"
" file. Useful for faster iteration when testing the import process before"
" including attachments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:184
msgid "``--allow-download`` / ``-l``: Allow downloading attachments from URLs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:185
msgid ""
"``--default-email-domain <DOMAIN>``: When a user's email is missing from "
"the export, generate one from their username and the provided domain "
"(e.g., ``--default-email-domain example.com``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:186
msgid ""
"``--skip-empty-emails``: Allow users with empty email addresses to be "
"included in the output. Note that this results in invalid import data "
"that will need to be manually corrected before importing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:187
msgid ""
"``--discard-invalid-props`` / ``-p``: Discard posts with invalid "
"properties. By default, such posts are kept but imported without their "
"properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:190
msgid "Debug transform"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:192
msgid ""
"The ``mmetl transform`` process produces a ``transform-slack.log`` file "
"that records INFO level output by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:194
msgid ""
"If you run the import commands with the ``--debug`` flag, the log will "
"include additional ``DEBUG`` level entries. These entries provide more "
"granular detail on each phase of the process, which can help identify "
"where the transformation may be slowing down or failing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:197
msgid "MMETL parsing phases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:199
msgid ""
"When parsing a Slack export file with the ``mmetl`` tool, the process "
"runs through four phases. You can track progress by monitoring the log "
"output during each phase. Understanding these phases helps set "
"expectations for how long the parsing step may take."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:201
msgid "**1. Reading the import file**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:203
msgid ""
"In this phase, ``mmetl`` reads through the Slack export file. Example log"
" line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:205
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``{\"file\":\"parse.go:359\",\"level\":\"info\",\"msg\":\"Processing file"
" 1 of 10335: aluminum-white-"
"lightbulb/\",\"time\":\"2024-03-11T20:41:09-04:00\"}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:207
msgid ""
"This step usually takes 5–10 minutes depending on the size of the export "
"archive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:209
msgid "**2. Converting user mentions**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:211
msgid ""
"During this phase, ``mmetl`` converts Slack user mentions into "
"Mattermost-compatible format. Example log line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:213
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``{\"file\":\"parse.go:224\",\"level\":\"debug\",\"msg\":\"Slack Import: "
"converting user mentions for channel touchscreen-headphones-sleek. 1 of "
"400\",\"time\":\"2024-03-11T20:41:10-04:00\"}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:215
msgid ""
"This step can be time-consuming on large imports and may take several "
"hours."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:217
msgid "**3. Converting channel mentions**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:219
msgid "In this phase, channel references are updated. Example log line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:221
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``{\"file\":\"parse.go:259\",\"level\":\"debug\",\"msg\":\"Slack Import: "
"converting channel mentions for channel robust-smart-home-device-matrix. "
"95 of 400\",\"time\":\"2024-03-11T20:41:48-04:00\"}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:223
msgid ""
"This step typically completes in about half the time required for user "
"mentions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:225
msgid "**4. Converting post markup**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:227
msgid ""
"Finally, Slack message formatting is converted into Mattermost-compatible"
" Markdown. Example log line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:229
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``{\"file\":\"parse.go:330\",\"level\":\"debug\",\"msg\":\"Slack Import: "
"converting markdown for channel vertex-robust-vacuum. 120 of "
"400\",\"time\":\"2024-03-11T20:41:58-04:00\"}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:231
msgid "This is the fastest step and usually completes quickly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:236
msgid "4. Import data into Mattermost"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/migrate-from-slack.rst:238
msgid ""
"You can upload the export through Mattermost's API from the server or "
"from another computer using mmctl commands. The server will save the "
"import in its file store before running the import (e.g. AWS S3), so "
"there will be time spent uploading/downloading the file in this case."
